   "rushing_attempts": "both quotes sit near HALF the book (Skattebo 5.45 v 11.5, Williams 7.38 v 17.5). That is the same \"about half the book\" signature the QB dropback audit found, and n=2, so it is a flag rather than a finding.",
   "receiving": "NOT a uniform shift. The model is BELOW on the top of each depth chart (Lamb -24.9%, Nabers -34.9%, Likely -58.8%) and ABOVE on the bottom (Theo Johnson +64.7%, Turpin +56.8%, Flournoy +51.1%). OLS of model on line has slope 0.686 (receiving yards) and 0.716 (receptions), and SD(model)/SD(line) is 0.790 and 0.930. The model COMPRESSES players toward the middle relative to the book."
